    <briefdescription>
<para>This class converts the costmap_2d into a set of lines (and points) </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The conversion is performed in three stages:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Clusters in the costmap are collected using the DBSCAN Algorithm (<ulink url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DBSCAN">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DBSCAN</ulink>) Reference: Ester, Martin; Kriegel, Hans-Peter; Sander, Jörg; Xu, Xiaowei, A density-based algorithm for discovering clusters in large spatial databases with noise. Proceedings of the Second International Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining. AAAI Press. 1996. pp. 226–231. ISBN 1-57735-004-9.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>In the subsequent stage, the convex hull of each cluster is determined using the monotone chain algorithm aka Andrew&apos;s algorithm: C++ implementation example: <ulink url="http://www.algorithmist.com/index.php/Monotone_Chain_Convex_Hull">http://www.algorithmist.com/index.php/Monotone_Chain_Convex_Hull</ulink> ( GNU Free Documentation License 1.2 ) Reference: A. M. Andrew, &quot;Another Efficient Algorithm for Convex Hulls in Two Dimensions&quot;, Info. Proc. Letters 9, 216-219 (1979).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>In the third step extract lines from each polygon (convex hull) if there exist at least a predefined number of support points.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>The output is a container of polygons (but each polygon does only contain a single vertex (point) or two vertices (line) </para>
    </detaileddescription>
